## Codebase Patterns

- **Deferred local-first enable**: `setSyncSubscriptions(true)` returns
  `pending` while `billingStatus.value === null` and applies automatically
  if an entitled billing status arrives. Callers that start bootstrap should
  only do so when the result is `applied`.
- **Disable/reset sync cancellation**: Destructive local-first flows should
  call `beginLocalFirstDisable(db)` before closing/removing local data and
  `endLocalFirstDisable(db)` only after the removal window is over.
  `runSync` treats that window as cancellation, aborts in-flight fetches,
  and suppresses sync-status error writes.
- **Bootstrap storage quota gate**: `bootstrapLocalDb` probes
  `navigator.storage.estimate()` before acquiring the local tab lock or
  opening SQLite. Low free space sets `bootstrapStorageWarning` and stops
  unless the caller supplies `confirmLowStorage` and the user confirms.
- **LWW equal timestamp tie-break**: Shared conflict checks should use
  `resolveLwwWrite(serverUpdatedAt, clientUpdatedAt)`. Server rows only win
  when their timestamp is strictly newer; equal timestamps accept the arriving
  client write. Local same-item `updateItem` rows are coalesced before push,
  so same-tick toggles send one final payload.
- **Add-feed dependent outbox rewrites**: When an optimistic `add_feed`
  reconciles to a canonical server id, update dependent pending operations
  that reference the optimistic feed id. `pushSync` snapshots outbox rows at
  drain start, so rewrite both SQLite rows and the in-memory queued rows
  before later operations in the same drain run.
- **State-level sync active gate**: Window `online` handlers should check
  `isLocalFirstActive.value` before looking up a cached DB or calling
  `runSync`. A cached local DB can briefly outlive the active UI state during
  disable/reset flows.
- **runSync concurrency**: App-level sync triggers should call `runSync`,
  not `pushSync`/`pullSync` directly. `runSync` owns the per-DB in-flight
  promise mutex so auth effects, online events, and manual triggers coalesce
  into one HTTP sync cycle.
- **Dev-login defense in depth**: `/api/auth/dev-login` must require
  `NODE_ENV === 'development'`, a loopback request hostname, and an explicit
  `SESSION_SECRET`. Server-side regression coverage for this route lives in
  `test/signup.ts`.
- **Worker secret bindings**: Production secrets such as
  `AUTUMN_SECRET_KEY` must be configured with `wrangler secret put`, not
  `wrangler.jsonc` `vars`. Static deployment checks belong in
  `test/deploy-config.mjs`, and `/api/health` should expose production
  config errors loudly.
- **Session cookie Secure flag**: Session cookies should call
  `shouldUseSecureSessionCookie(c.req.url)` in `src/server/index.ts`.
  The flag is true for every non-loopback hostname and false only for
  loopback development hosts; do not key it off `NODE_ENV`.
- **Billing dev shortcut fail-closed**: The no-Autumn billing shortcut is
  allowed only when `NODE_ENV === 'development'`. Tests that exercise that
  shortcut should set `NODE_ENV` explicitly; production or test envs without
  live Autumn config should return `503 billing_unavailable`.
- **Cached local DB ownership**: `getLocalDb(did)` must only return the
  cached SQLite handle while `getTabCoordinationState() === 'primary'`.
  A blocked tab can still have an old cached adapter/DB from an earlier
  lock, but state-level sync must treat it as remote until `getAdapter()`
  reacquires the local tab lock.
- **SQLite OPFS probe/open reuse**: A successful `probeOpfsSupport()`
  keeps its `SQLiteWorkerClient` for the next `openLocalDb()` call, and
  the worker caches the installed OPFS-SAH pool by directory. Test resets
  that swap worker factories or return to in-memory mode should dispose
  the cached probe worker.
- **OPFS tab coordination authority**: `acquireLocalTabLock()` uses the
  Web Locks API lock named `rsss-opfs` as the primary-tab source of truth.
  `BroadcastChannel('rsss-tab')` remains only a compatibility/status hint;
  release adapter-held locks through `releaseLocalTabLock()` and await it
  when immediately retrying local DB open paths.
- **Local write timestamp source**: Client local-first writes should compute
  one `const now = formatSqliteTs(new Date())` per mutation and bind that
  value into both affected row `updated_at` columns and the outbox
  `client_updated_at`. Do not mix a JS timestamp with SQL `datetime('now')`
  in the same mutation.
- **Update-item outbox coalescing**: Local `updateItem` writes should keep
  one pending `update_item` outbox row per item and merge new payload values
  into it. Build the payload from the row after the SQL update so booleans
  preserve false values and match the local state that will be pushed.
- **Bootstrap failure classification**: `bootstrapLocalDb` treats fetch
  rejection, abort, 5xx, unavailable storage, and local-tab lock failures as
  transient. Transient failures keep `syncSubscriptions` enabled, keep OPFS
  data in place, and set `bootstrapRetryAvailable`; destructive cleanup must
  stay behind the terminal-confirmation branch.
- **Paginated sync cursoring**: `/api/sync` returns `hasMore` and an
  opaque `nextCursor`; `pullSync` persists that cursor in `sync_meta` after
  each committed page and clears it only when the final page advances
  `last_pull_at`. Bootstrap progress should use page callbacks rather than
  per-row callbacks.
- **Skipped pull rows block cursor advancement**: When `pullSync` skips
  rows protected by pending outbox operations, it must leave
  `last_pull_at` unchanged and avoid persisting later cursors. The server
  filters with `updated_at > since`, so advancing past a skipped row can
  make that row unreachable after the outbox clears.
- **Local-first a11y/CSS regression checks**:
  `test/local-first-a11y-static.mjs` owns static checks for the local-first
  settings and sync status surface, including live status semantics,
  `aria-describedby` wiring, no border-radius, and variable-only colors.
- **Local-first PWA docs**: v1 ships a web app manifest but no service
  worker. Keep service worker claims out of README/DOCS until an actual
  worker and registration exist; `test/local-first-docs.mjs` owns the static
  regression assertions.
- **Local DB failure surface**: `openLocalDb` classifies failures with
  `classifyLocalDbError`; adapter selection stores user-facing recovery state
  in `localDbError`. Quota/corruption should return `remoteAdapter` with a
  visible Settings error instead of silently falling back.
- **OPFS removal ordering**: Disable/reset/bootstrap-failure cleanup should
  close the active local SQLite handle with `closeDb(db)` before calling
  `removeOpfsDb(did)`.
- **Bootstrap failure cleanup hook**: Cross-module in-memory cleanup for
  bootstrap failures is registered through `addBootstrapFailureCleanup`.
  Use it instead of importing `db/index.ts` from `bootstrap.ts`.
- **Content storage opt-out**: Turning `storeContent` off purges local
  `items.content` and `items.description` through `purgeStoredContent(db)`.
  Keep future toggle-off flows wired to that helper so old article bodies do
  not remain in OPFS.
- **Reader missing-content fallback**: `State.loadItemByRoute` preserves the
  local item row and only fills missing `content`/`description` from the
  remote route endpoint when a local-first route item has no body and the
  browser is online. Do not overwrite local optimistic read/starred state
  with the remote fetch.
- **Outbox retry idempotency**: `pushSync` sends `client_op_id` on every
  outbox request. The server does not store processed ops in v1; add-feed
  retries reconcile by unique feed URL, delete-feed retries with a missing
  row return success, and item/mark-all-read writes are idempotent value
  assignments.
- **Outbox failure classification**: 5xx and network failures are transient
  retry/backoff state and must not move rows to `dead_letter_outbox`.
  Permanent 4xx responses other than 401/402/409 dead-letter immediately;
  401/402 throw and preserve the outbox row.
- **Push conflict response contract**: Server 409 responses are wrapped as
  `{ feed }`, `{ item }`, or `{ items }`. Client 409 handling should extract
  those authoritative rows, upsert them locally, then clear the matching
  outbox row.
- **Post-sync UI refresh**: State-level sync completion should call
  `State.refreshAfterSync(state)`. It reloads feeds, items, counts, and the
  currently open `/post/*` route item after a successful sync cycle.
- **Sync error counts**: `runSync` should refresh outbox and dead-letter
  counts before setting sync error state, so a successful push attempt is
  reflected even when a later pull step fails.
- **Lazy SQLite Vite packaging**: Keep the client build input to
  `index.html`. The SQLite worker and WASM assets are emitted from
  `new Worker(new URL('./sqlite-worker.ts', import.meta.url))` and the
  worker's dynamic `import('@sqlite.org/sqlite-wasm')`; do not add
  `sqlite-init` as a standalone Vite entry.
- **Local-first support detection**: `isLocalFirstSupported()` is async and
  must confirm OPFS through the SQLite worker probe before returning true.
  Settings UI should read the `localFirstSupported` signal; do not gate local
  first on main-thread `FileSystemSyncAccessHandle`.
- **SQLite worker bridge testing**: Keep the mockable
  `SQLiteWorkerClient` separate from the Vite-specific worker factory that
  uses `new URL(..., import.meta.url)`. Browser-bundled tapout tests can
  import the client without esbuild `import.meta` warnings, while app code can
  import the factory for lazy worker packaging.
- **Worker-backed local DB calls**: Production local SQLite handles may be
  worker-backed and asynchronous. Shared local-first code should use
  `execDb`, `queryDb`, and `queryOneDb` instead of direct synchronous
  `db.exec` when it must work in both production and in-memory tests.
- **Client routing helpers**: Pure item-route helpers live in
  `src/client/routing.ts` and use canonical `Item` types from
  `src/client/db/types.ts`. `state.ts` re-exports these helpers for legacy
  component imports, but new routing tests should import the helper module
  directly.
- **Billing email app links**: Route handlers should pass request-origin
  `baseUrl` into subscription billing emails. Email templates should derive
  in-app links with `new URL(path, baseUrl)` so text and HTML never emit
  relative URLs.
- **README deploy command tests**: `test/readme-deploy.mjs` owns static
  deploy-doc assertions, including current Wrangler KV namespace syntax.
  Keep README deployment command regressions in that Node test.
- **Server route static tests**: Repository-level route-shape assertions can
  live in `test/server-routing-static.mjs` and should be listed in
  `test/run-all-tests.mjs` so route cleanup regressions are covered without
  browser bundling.
- **Local-first delete/reset preflight**: Disable/reset flows should call
  `pushSync` before removing OPFS data, then verify `getOutboxCount(db)`.
  `pushSync` records retryable failures without throwing, so pending rows
  after a drain must be treated as a `LocalFirstSyncFailureError`.
- **Component tests with CSS imports**: Browser tests that bundle Preact
  components importing CSS need `esbuild --loader:.css=text`; otherwise
  esbuild fails before tapout can run the component assertions.
- **Client lifecycle cleanup**: `AppState` exposes `cleanup()` for listeners
  and other lifecycle resources created by `State()`. Module entrypoints
  should call it from teardown hooks such as `import.meta.hot.dispose`.
- **Repository configuration tests**: Focused repository-level assertions can
  live in `.mjs` files under `test/` and be listed in
  `test/run-all-tests.mjs` before browser-bundled tapout tests.
- **Client route static tests**: Client route source-shape and documentation
  regressions can live in focused `.mjs` tests under `test/`; wire them into
  `test/run-all-tests.mjs` so the full suite catches drift.
- **Client Feed/Item type authority**: `src/client/db/types.ts` owns the
  canonical client `Feed` and `Item` interfaces. `state.ts` imports and
  re-exports those types for existing UI imports instead of redefining them.
- **Local content caching scope**: Feed-level local caching is not supported.
  Use the local-first `storeContent` setting for article content storage;
  do not add `is_locally_cached` or per-feed cache toggles.
- **Client auth state authority**: `state.user` is the authoritative client
  auth state. Do not persist duplicate user objects under the legacy
  `rsss_user` localStorage key.
- **Autumn subscription status narrowing**: `verifySubscription` should
  treat Autumn SDK statuses as untrusted runtime values and narrow them
  through a local type guard before returning app-level billing state.
- **Autumn customer email source**: Live checkout should stash the email
  returned by `getOrCreateCustomer`; notification routes read the pending
  email from KV instead of re-fetching the same Autumn customer record.
- **Session cookie format**: Session cookies use
  `<payloadB64>.<signatureB64>`, where `payloadB64` is URL-safe base64 JSON
  containing only `{ sid }`. Sign and verify the encoded payload segment
  with the HMAC helper; load session data from KV via `session:${sid}`.
- **Isolation headers for iframe compatibility**: Use
  `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless` with
  `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` in both Vite dev headers and
  `src/server/isolation-headers.ts`. This preserves cross-origin isolation
  while allowing third-party iframe embeds that are blocked by `require-corp`.
- **Sync status orchestration**: App-level sync cycles should use
  `runSync` from `src/client/db/sync.ts`. It owns `setSyncDone`; pass
  `{ trackStatus: false }` only from orchestrators that will set final
  sync status themselves.
- **Sync auth expiry handling**: `pullSync` and `pushSync` expose typed auth
  errors. `runSync` rethrows them without setting generic sync-error status;
  `State.handleSyncAuthError` owns clearing auth state and routing to login.
- **Durable Object route tests**: Route behavior can be tested without a real
  DO instance by using `Object.create(UserDO.prototype)`, assigning a focused
  fake `sql` object and `ctx.waitUntil`, then calling the private
  `createRouter()` through a typed test shim.
- **Durable Object migration cache**: Server-only DO migrations are gated by
  `schema_migration` in DO storage. Bump `USER_DO_MIGRATION_VERSION` whenever
  a new introspective DO migration is added so existing objects rerun checks.
- **Feed parser tests**: Durable Object parser behavior can be tested without
  constructing a DO by importing `UserDO`, creating
  `Object.create(UserDO.prototype)`, and calling the private parser through a
  typed test shim. Browser-bundled tests that import the DO need the
  `cloudflare:workers` esbuild alias.
- **Tapout browser tests**: Tapout uses a fixed local port, so focused
  browser test commands must run serially rather than in parallel.
- **Forbidden browser headers in tests**: Chromium-based tapout tests cannot
  set forbidden request headers such as `Cookie`, `Origin`, or
  `Sec-Fetch-Site`. Keep security decisions in pure helpers, and use a small
  Hono wrapper that sets variables directly when middleware tests need
  authenticated request context.
- **Bounded feed reads**: `fetchFeedText` requires `response.body` and reads
  through a stream with the byte cap. Do not fall back to `response.text()`.
- **Schema split pattern**: The shared schema exports `TABLES_SQL`, `INDEXES_SQL`, `TRIGGERS_SQL`, and `SCHEMA_SQL` (combined). The DO must apply them in order: tables → server migrations → indexes/triggers. Client (OPFS) can use `SCHEMA_SQL` directly on a fresh DB.
- **SQLite foreign keys**: `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;` is connection-local.
  Run it immediately after opening any client or Durable Object SQLite handle,
  before applying schema or relying on `ON DELETE CASCADE`.

- **Test command**: `npm run test:db` runs `test/db-adapter.ts` via esbuild + tapout in a browser (Chromium). All DB adapter interface tests live there.
- **Import paths**: TypeScript source uses `.js` extensions in imports (e.g. `../../shared/schema.js`) for ESM compatibility with esbuild.
- **sqlite-wasm in tapout tests**: tapout's HTTP server only serves the test bundle. To use sqlite-wasm in tests, use `--loader:.wasm=dataurl` with esbuild (inlines WASM as base64), import the wasm as `import wasmUrl from '@sqlite.org/sqlite-wasm/sqlite3.wasm'`, and pass `{ locateFile: () => wasmUrl }` to `sqlite3Module.default()`. Use `setTestMode(true, wasmUrl)` before tests to enable in-memory mode.
- **Server feed fetch security**: Feed fetches should go through
  `src/server/feed-fetch.ts` so URL validation, fetch timeout, and the
  5MB response cap stay centralized.
- **OPFS tab coordination**: Local-first OPFS ownership is coordinated in
  `src/client/db/tab-coordination.ts` with BroadcastChannel `rsss-tab`.
  Check this coordinator before opening SQLite so second tabs fall back to
  `remoteAdapter` instead of contending for the exclusive OPFS lock.
- **API routing boundary**: Entitlement-gated data routes are mounted through
  exported `dataRouter` in `src/server/index.ts`. Auth and billing routes stay
  on the main `app`; new user data endpoints should inherit
  `dataRouter.use('*', requireAuth)` and
  `dataRouter.use('*', requireEntitlement)`.
- **Dynamic Hono status codes**: When returning dynamic numeric statuses from
  server helper errors through `c.json`, narrow them at the response boundary
  with Hono's `ContentfulStatusCode` type so typecheck remains strict.
- **Local-first sync cycle order**: Use `src/client/db/sync-cycle.ts` for
  app-triggered sync cycles. It runs `pushSync` before `pullSync` so pending
  optimistic writes reach the server before remote rows are merged locally.
  Keep `getPendingOutboxRefs` on the pull side after `pushSync` resolves,
  otherwise stale `mark_all_read` refs can hide newly pulled server items.
- **Pending outbox pull protection**: `pullSync` skips server rows covered by
  pending outbox operations (`update_item`, `mark_all_read`, `add_feed`,
  `delete_feed`) so stale pulls cannot overwrite local optimistic writes.
- **Optimistic feed ID reconciliation**: On successful `add_feed` push,
  delete the optimistic local feed row before upserting the server feed row.
  Do this in one transaction because `feeds.url` is unique.
- **Dead-letter outbox status**: `pushSync` owns promotion from `outbox`
  to `dead_letter_outbox` and updates `syncDeadLetters`; status UI reads that
  signal instead of querying SQLite directly.
- **Durable Object alarm refreshes**: Keep alarm feed polling bounded through
  `refreshFeeds` with `FEED_REFRESH_CONCURRENCY` instead of unbounded
  `Promise.all`; always await `ctx.storage.setAlarm` when rescheduling.
- **Feed fetch failures**: Server feed rows include `last_error` and
  `last_status`; update both from `fetchFeed` failures so failed refreshes are
  queryable after alarm or manual refresh runs.
- **Client SQLite timestamps**: Client-side SQLite writes should use
  `formatSqliteTs(new Date())` for JS-generated timestamps, or
  `datetime('now')` inside SQL. Do not write ISO strings into SQLite timestamp
  columns or outbox `client_updated_at`.
- **Billing email retries**: `sendSubscriptionStarted` and
  `sendPaymentFailed` accept a Worker retry context; pass `c.executionCtx`
  from request handlers so transient Resend failures retry through
  `waitUntil`.

- **Article route matching**: Use `itemRouteCandidates` from
  `src/shared/item-route.ts` for article link lookup. It builds exact link
  candidates for trailing-slash and `http`/`https` variants; do not use
  substring matching or SQL `LIKE` for `/post/*` article routes.
- **DEBUG storage seeding**: Use `configureDebugStorage` from
  `src/client/debug-storage.ts` for app DEBUG localStorage handling. Dev and
  staging should seed the default only when missing; production should remove
  only the app-seeded default value.

- **OPFS persistence browser coverage**: Tapout browser tests do not provide
  a real cross-origin-isolated OPFS environment. Use
  `setSQLiteWorkerClientFactoryForTests` with a persistent worker-backed fake
  for CI coverage, and keep a manual browser script for the real OPFS file
  check.
- **Aggregate tests with sqlite-wasm**: If a test imported through
  `test/index.ts` imports `@sqlite.org/sqlite-wasm/sqlite3.wasm`,
  `test/run-all-tests.mjs` must pass `--loader:.wasm=dataurl` to esbuild.

